Found during the k45/k141 review. With no agent configured, the launcher stays up after the editor gives up, as long as MCP is serving (k69): a retry can still come through MCP. If serving then fails (decision on k45: a serve failure after the bind logs an ERROR and does not exit), nothing checks again. The launcher idles with no editor, no agent and no MCP until Ctrl-C or q.

Done when: in that state (no agent, editor given up, MCP no longer serving) the launcher ends with exit 1 the same way the k69 rule does for MCP off, whichever of the two events comes second, with a test for both orders. Rare; low priority.

**Decision 2026-11-21 (main agent):** as the card says. With no agent, the editor given up and MCP no longer serving, the launcher ends with exit 1 by the k69 rule, in either order, with a test for each order. The log line names both reasons. Worker in its own worktree; main.go/lifecycle.go run one after another.

