Logic, OK: the lock makes exactly one of the two events end the session (give-up reads serving under the lock, serveMCP clears serving before mcpStopped locks). All starts (ue_start, ue_restart, console start/r, autostart, restart-policy backoff) run start() and PreStart, so started() clears. With an agent gaveUp is false and nothing is recorded (k45 kept). A normal close/Ctrl-C returns ErrServerClosed (Serve also returns it when Accept fails during shutdown), and httpSrv.Close only runs after the session ended, so finishLocked would ignore a fail anyway.
