1. (worker) main_test.go:576-587 TestServeMCPClosedIsNotAFailure ignores serveMCP's new result. My mutation 'return true on close' survives every test. Effect today: only a stray k155 line after a shutdown with a waiting give-up; the exit code is safe. Assert false there, and true in TestServeMCPFailureMarksMCPNotServingAndSaysSo (main_test.go:524).
2. (main agent, README) README.md:1491 'a launcher with no agent whose editor has given up' is wider than the code. README:423 calls every failure without restart a give-up, but a run that failed after more than 10 s is not ended by k155. Say e.g. 'whose editor's last run was a quick failure with no restart following (see Exit codes)'. README:404 and :419 are correct in context.
Item 3 race: real but microseconds wide. A start must reach the loop after the exit branch's peek at svc.ctrl (a start already waiting there suppresses OnExit) and before the OnExit goroutine takes the lock. It hurts only if a non-temporary Accept failure comes later, which is itself rare. Then exit 1 would kill a running editor. Accept as negligible; optionally one sentence at lifecycle.go:253-254 naming the window. If it is ever closed: keep the flag, and also check the supervisor at serve-failure time (end only when ue is neither Running nor Unresponsive/pre-start). Status alone cannot replace the flag: it cannot tell a quick-failure give-up from a long run that failed, a manual stop, manualStart or a pending backoff.
Item 2 (ERROR line, then 'stopping everything'): leave it. No agent means no window mode, so both lines are adjacent on one console, the second names the outcome, and README documents 'right after that line'. Changing it means reordering serveMCP's logging and re-pinning its test.
